  "summary": "The study fabricated LiF/HCl-MILD-derived Ti3C2Tx interdigitated flexible microsupercapacitors on PI, using PVA/H2SO4 gel for pseudocapacitive sensing. Two distinct electrode architectures are reported: the buffered MXene FMSC/Pseudocapacitive Sensor and a no-PVA-buffer control device. The primary sensor achieved its best reported volumetric capacitance of 1293.27 F cm\u22123 in the released state using 2 M PVA/H2SO4 at 10 mV s\u22121. The no-buffer control reached an initial 946.3 F cm\u22123, but its electrolyte concentration and CV scan rate are not specified in the supplied main text."
